## Fallible Conversions

```xiom
pub interface TryFrom[Src] {
  type Error;
  fn try_from(value: Src) -> Result[Self, Self::Error];
}
```

### Implementing TryFrom

```xiom
pub type PositiveInt = Int;

pub type ConversionError = enum {
  NotPositive,
  Overflow,
}

impl TryFrom[Int] for PositiveInt {
  type Error = ConversionError;

  fn try_from(n: Int) -> Result[PositiveInt, ConversionError] {
    if n <= 0 { return Err(ConversionError::NotPositive); }
    return Ok(n);
  }
}

fn main() {
  match PositiveInt::try_from(5) {
    Ok(p) => io.println("Valid: " + p.to_str()),
    Err(_) => io.println("Invalid input"),
  }
}
```

### Parsing Strings

```xiom
pub type Port = Int;

impl TryFrom[Str] for Port {
  type Error = Str;

  fn try_from(s: Str) -> Result[Port, Str] {
    let n = s.parse_int()?;
    if n < 1 || n > 65535 {
      return Err("Port must be 1-65535");
    }
    return Ok(n);
  }
}
```

### Using ? with TryFrom

```xiom
fn parse_config(raw: Str) -> Result[Config, ConversionError] {
  let port: Port = raw.parse_int()?.into();  // Chained TryFrom
  let timeout: Seconds = raw.parse_int()?.into();
  return Ok(Config{ port: port, timeout: timeout });
}
```

### Blanket Into from TryFrom

Just like From → Into, implementing TryFrom automatically gives you TryInto.

